            <h2 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold text-[#102046] mt-5 mb-8">
                Can AI-generated language escape the biases embedded in human language?
            </h2>

            <div class="max-w-3xl text-slate-700 leading-8 space-y-5">

                <p>
                    Language is not simply a neutral tool for
                    communication. Word choices, descriptions,
                    and recurring expressions can reflect
                    broader social values and cultural expectations.
                </p>

                <p>
                    Some assumptions become embedded in
                    everyday linguistic conventions. When
                    particular ways of describing people and
                    social roles become dominant, they can
                    gradually be treated as ordinary or universal.
                </p>

                <p>
                    The increasing use of AI-generated language
                    raises another question: when AI systems
                    generate text based on existing linguistic
                    patterns, do they also reproduce the
                    assumptions embedded in human language?
                </p>

                <p>
                    This research examined systemic bias in
                    human and AI-generated language through
                    qualitative analysis and interviews. It
                    considered how dominant linguistic norms
                    may influence social representation,
                    particularly in relation to gender.
                </p>

            </div>

        </section>



